\par\par \b \uc2 Strong Labor Market Confronts Omicron --- Jobless claims trend near a half-century low, but impact of variant remains uncertain\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gwynn Guilford and Bryan Mena \par \uc2 940 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 December 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 U.S. employers added a record number of jobs in 2021, as a gauge of layoffs fell to a half-century low and available positions surged on strong demand for labor during the economy's recovery from pandemic-related shutdowns.\par \par \uc2 But the pace of labor market gains could slow early next year due to the uncertainty posed by the Covid-19 Omicron variant, especially in restaurants, hotels and other venues where people gather.\par \par \uc2 Applications for unemployment benefits, a proxy for layoffs, have trended near five-decade lows in recent weeks. Jobless claims for the week ended Dec. 25 fell from the prior week to a seasonally adjusted 198,000, the Labor Department said Thursday. Last week's four-week moving average, which smooths out volatility, fell to the lowest level since October 1969.\par \par \uc2 Strong job creation has been a cornerstone of 2021's robust economic growth and would be relied upon to underpin gains next year in the face of headwinds tied to the prolonged pandemic, elevated inflation and supply shortages.\par \par \uc2 Jobless claims will be closely watched in the coming weeks for any signs that the Omicron variant is causing employers to lay off workers. Claims data, which are reported weekly, are often an early signal that hiring, and the broader economy, is shifting.\par \par \uc2 "So far we haven't seen a noticeable impact from Omicron on labor market data, at least in terms of the claims data," said \uc2 Nancy Vanden Houten\uc2 , lead U.S. economist at Oxford Economics, adding that a recent Census survey also showed no big increase in the number of firms reducing workers.\par \par \uc2 "I think businesses are striving to remain open, particularly given the evidence that Omicron produces milder symptoms," she said. Still, she said, the variant could cause an uptick in claims in the weeks ahead.\par \par \uc2 Oxford Economics expects employers to add five million payroll jobs in 2022, equal to an average of more than 400,000 a month. That would be a modest slowdown from this year, when U.S. employers added an average of 555,000 a month, or 6.1 million jobs through the first 11 months of 2021, according to the Labor Department. This year's job increase is already the largest on record back to 1940.\par \par \uc2 The unemployment rate is on track to dip to 3.7% by the fourth quarter of next year, said \uc2 Ms. Vanden Houten\uc2  -- slightly above the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's projection for the end of next year. The unemployment rate was 4.2% in November.\par \par \uc2 Pantheon Macroeconomics, another forecasting firm, expects employers to add 450,000 jobs a month, on average, in 2022, and for the unemployment rate to average 3.5% in the fourth quarter. \uc2 PNC Financial Services Group\uc2  projects an average of 350,000 jobs to be added monthly next year, and for the jobless rate to decline to 3.8% by the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 Omicron "might change the pattern of growth with somewhat weaker job growth in the first few months of the year, and then stronger job growth after that," PNC Chief Economist \uc2 Gus Faucher\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 So far there are only signs of a modest economic impact due to the variant. Airline flights have been grounded due to lack of crews, hockey and basketball games have been canceled, some businesses have temporarily closed or shifted back to remote work and public schools have moved to online-only in early January. Some economists have downgraded forecasts for growth for early next year.\par \par \uc2 Another constraint on employment and economic growth next year could be the shrunken labor force, which has nearly 2.5 million fewer workers than before the pandemic. Job openings exceeded unemployed workers by 3.6 million in October, according to the latest available data from the Labor Department.\par \par \uc2 That has left employers clamoring for workers, raising pay and sweetening bonuses and benefits -- and in some cases looking to different types of workers than they have in the past.\par \par \uc2 Tusco Display is short of the workers it needs to meet demand, Chief Executive Michael Lauber said. He has responded by seeking out part-time workers.\par \par \uc2 "We still would prefer to hire people on a full-time basis," Mr. Lauber said. "But there's a substantial number of people out there who for whatever reason -- maybe it's elder care, maybe it's child care, maybe it's who knows what -- are not able or willing to take a full-time position."\par \par \uc2 The Gnadenhutten, Ohio, company, which makes custom store displays, has stepped up recruitment of students, with nine high-school students joining Tusco doing light assembly work in the afternoons and evenings last week.\par \par \uc2 The company also recently recruited a trio of young welding students from vocational programs. Mr. Lauber said he hopes to expand this team in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Labor-supply constraints and the evolving pandemic, however, are unlikely to derail labor-market improvements in 2022, said \uc2 Bernard Baumohl\uc2 , chief global economist of the Economic Outlook Group LLC.\par \par \uc2 "Our expectation is that the economy is going to continue to be strong," he said. He projects better hiring next year than in 2021, forecasting an average of 650,000 jobs to be added monthly.\par \par \uc2 Workers have gained leverage, Mr. Baumohl said, and that means they have become selective in the kinds of employment opportunities they find suitable. Self-employment has also increased.\par \par \uc2 "They're entrepreneurs and they've started their own business at a time when they thought they now have some financial resources to do so," he said.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw380\pich236\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal5700\pichgoal3540
