\par\par \uc2 The Property Report\par \b \uc2 Chicago Tower Sells To Oak Hill\b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Grant \par \uc2 469 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 December 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 The last name of Matt Borstein, who heads a real-estate unit for Oak Hill Advisors, was misspelled as Bornstein in a Property Report article on Wednesday about a Chicago office tower.\par \par \uc2 (WSJ Dec. 30, 2021)\par \par \uc2 (END)\par \par \uc2 A venture led by \uc2 Oak Hill Advisors\uc2  agreed to buy a controlling interest in a new 55-story office tower in Chicago in the latest sign that investors are paying up for modern, amenity-rich office buildings despite uncertainty over the return-to-office.\par \par \uc2 Oak Hill agreed to buy 110 North Wacker Drive from \uc2 Howard Hughes Corp\uc2 . in a deal that values the 1.5-million-square-foot skyscraper at more than $1 billion, according to people familiar with the matter. It would be the highest price paid for a Chicago property building since the beginning of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The deal, scheduled to close next year, comes as the office-building industry is being split into haves and have-nots by the pandemic's work-from-home trend. Owners of trophy space with great views and state-of-the-art air filtration have been attracting tenants looking for ways to lure their workers back to offices.\par \par \uc2 But leasing volume remains anemic for more ordinary space, especially as the Omicron variant delays return-to-office plans. Demand may not return to pre-pandemic levels even after the Covid-19 virus is tamed because many businesses are adopting "hybrid" workplace strategies that allow employees to work from home part of the time.\par \par \uc2 Located on the Chicago River, 110 N. Wacker opened in October 2020 with a 45-foot lobby, numerous dining options and a secondary air-filtration system that was added during the pandemic. The space is over 85% leased by tenants including \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  and law firm Morgan Lewis.\par \par \uc2 Howard Hughes, a real-estate development company with roots dating back to the storied pilot and business tycoon, decided in 2019 to put noncore assets up for sale. Earlier this year, the company hired the Chicago office of Eastdil Secured LLC to market 110 N. Wacker as part of that program.\par \par \uc2 "We're going to wait for the right price, not the first price," said \uc2 David O'Reilly\uc2 , Howard Hughes chief executive, on an earnings call with analysts in November.\par \par \uc2 Other trophy office properties are fetching high prices. \uc2 Blackstone Inc\uc2 . is in advanced talks to acquire a 49% stake in a two-year-old New York office tower named One Manhattan West in a deal that values the skyscraper at $2.85 billion.\par \par \uc2 Oak Hill has been an active buyer of commercial property since it formed a new real-estate unit last year headed by Matt Bornstein, the former global head of \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's commercial real-estate business.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020211229ehct00037\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
