\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: New York Times Strikes First Deal With Wirecutter Workers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Allison Prang \par \uc2 383 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 December 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B7\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Wirecutter Union said it has reached a deal on its first collective-bargaining agreement with the \uc2 New York Times Co\uc2  . after staffers for the product-review site went on strike last month during the busy holiday shopping season.\par \par \uc2 The Wirecutter Union said the contract includes average wage increases of about $5,000 and that its lowest paid staffers will get raises of 18% immediately. The three-year contract also includes minimum guaranteed pay increases of between 2% to 2.5% a year, according to the union.\par \par \uc2 Increases on union members' healthcare costs are also capped and the agreement includes a ban on nondisclosure agreements referencing harassment or discrimination, the union said.\par \par \uc2 "Our members at Wirecutter love what they do, and now they will be fairly paid for their work," NewsGuild of New York President Susan DeCarava said in prepared remarks.\par \par \uc2 Wirecutter is a product-recommendation website that the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  acquired in 2016. The Times put Wirecutter behind a paywall in September.\par \par \uc2 "We're very pleased that The Times Company has reached an agreement in principle with the Wirecutter Union," \uc2 Danielle Rhoades Ha\uc2  , a spokeswoman for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , said in an email. She said members of the Wirecutter bargaining unit still have to vote on the deal.\par \par \uc2 The contract ends two years of negotiations between the company and union. The first bargaining session was in December 2019, according to Nick Guy, unit chair of the Wirecutter Union and a senior staff writer for the site.\par \par \uc2 Union members went on strike from Thanksgiving Day through Cyber Monday, a period the union calls the site's most profitable time of the year, and asked people not to shop on the site during that period.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  said in late November that Wirecutter had its best month for total audience in the site's 10-year history.\par \par \uc2 The workers' strike garnered monetary support. A \uc2 GoFundMe\uc2  campaign started by Mr. Guy raised more than $42,000 to help cover pay that workers missed out on by participating in the strike.\par \par \uc2 The Wirecutter Union is represented by the NewsGuild of New York, with which the union that represents many employees at The Wall Street Journal is also affiliated.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020211215ehcf0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
