\par\par \uc2 Heard on the Street\par \b \uc2 The Future of Offices Isn't Just About Working From Home\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carol Ryan \par \uc2 599 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 November 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B14\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 [Financial Analysis and Commentary]\par \par \uc2 It is tempting to see home working as the big threat to city-center offices. But investors might gain more by watching an old real-estate fundamental: construction.\par \par \uc2 Compare London and New York. Few new offices were started in the U.K. capital in recent years, partly as a result of Brexit, which should help big commercial landlords there recover relatively quickly from the pandemic. Faced with a building glut, their peers in New York may not be so lucky.\par \par \uc2 Real-estate investment trusts \uc2 British Land\uc2 , \uc2 Great Portland Estates\uc2  and \uc2 Landsec\uc2 , which own office portfolios in London, all noted a pickup in lease signings over the three months through September. The three companies also said the value of their Central London office portfolios increased by between 1.6% and 2.8% over six months.\par \par \uc2 Overall take-up of offices in London was still 12% below average quarterly levels in the third quarter, according to real-estate broker Knight Frank. But corporate tenants that had delayed decisions about adding space while their workers were restricted to working from home are starting to commit to new leases. \uc2 Facebook\uc2  signed one of London's bigger deals of the period, taking on a building in the city's West End.\par \par \uc2 The office market is splitting in two: Energy-efficient buildings in central locations are in demand as tenants try to lure employees back to the workplace and meet "net-zero" targets for carbon emissions. Meanwhile, older offices are increasingly difficult to fill.\par \par \uc2 Of all the London leases signed since the pandemic began, six in 10 have been for new or newly renovated offices, according to Knight Frank, compared with under four in 10 over the decade before the crisis. The vacancy rate across all Central London offices currently stands at 9.1%, \uc2 British Land\uc2  reported, while it is just 3.5% for so-called prime buildings. These best-in-class offices make up only around 10% to 20% of the city's total stock, yet big listed landlords own a disproportionate share of them, as well as older buildings in good locations that can be refurbished.\par \par \uc2 Tight supply means owners of prime buildings can expect healthy interest. Construction of new office blocks in London slowed after 2016 as developers tried to understand how the U.K.'s vote to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2  would affect the capital. Only 8 million square feet of speculative new offices will be built between now and 2025, compared with projected take-up of 4.7 million square feet a year.\par \par \uc2 New York's major listed landlords like SL Green and \uc2 Empire State Realty Trust\uc2  face a harsher reality. Between 2022 and 2024, 25 million square feet of new office construction or major renovations will hit the Manhattan market -- the most in any three-year period since the 1980s, calculates Franklin Wallach, director at real-estate firm Colliers.\par \par \uc2 While Manhattan-based corporate tenants seem as interested in moving into the newest and most sustainable offices, there are too many buildings available for landlords to capitalize on the trend. By the end of the third quarter, 17% of Manhattan prewar office space was available to rent. But the rate was even higher for locations built since 2015, at 18%, according to Colliers data.\par \par \uc2 The pandemic's long-term impact on corporate demand for prime office space remains murky. What is clear is that big landlords will have more new buildings on their hands in New York than in London.\par \par \uc2 page,5043 \par \par \uc2 Document J000000020211124ehbo0001e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
