\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Zoom Sales Growth Loses Momentum --- Videoconferencing demand eases as more people return to the workplace\b0\par\par\uc2 By Aaron Tilley \par \uc2 420 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 November 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Zoom Video Communications Inc\uc2 . sales growth slowed last quarter as the extra demand for remote work and the company's videoconferencing application eased, along with a pullback in the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The San Jose, Calif., company said sales rose 35% from a year earlier to $1.05 billion for the three months ended Oct. 31. In the previous quarter, the company's sales rose 54%. A year earlier, its sales jumped more than 360%.\par \par \uc2 Zoom's net income for its fiscal third quarter rose more than 70% from a year earlier to $340 million. Analysts projected sales of $1.02 billion and net income of $337 million.\par \par \uc2 For its current quarter ending in January, Zoom expects total sales between $1.051 billion and $1.053 billion, better than the $1.018 billion expected by Wall Street, according to FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Zoom were down 5.9% at $228 in after-hours trading.\par \par \uc2 Zoom has been unable to maintain the heady growth it experienced when organizations leaned heavily into remote work after the onset of Covid-19. Amid the pandemic, Zoom's sales shot up fourfold from the previous year.\par \par \uc2 The company also faces increased competition. \uc2 Microsoft Corp\uc2 .'s Teams application, which combines videoconferencing and other collaboration features, poses one of the biggest challenges to Zoom's market share.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  said in July that Teams had reached record levels, with nearly 250 million monthly active users. \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  also intends to bring Teams to every Windows user as part of its next-generation operating system now being rolled out.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Meta Platforms Inc\uc2 ., formerly called \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , are planning the next steps of what remote-collaboration workspaces could look like through virtual worlds known as the metaverse.\par \par \uc2 Some investors are concerned that Zoom's best days are behind it unless it finds new businesses. The value of Zoom's shares are down more than 40% from a year ago.\par \par \uc2 Other companies such as \uc2 Peloton Interactive Inc\uc2 . that experienced sizable gains during the pandemic's initial stay-at-home phase have also struggled to maintain growth as businesses and schools reopen.\par \par \uc2 Some of Zoom's diversification plans have been thwarted. In September, the company's nearly $15 billion offer to acquire the cloud call-center business \uc2 Five9 Inc\uc2 . was abandoned over differences in price.\par \par \uc2 The deal also faced a Justice Department-led investigation over potential national-security risks presented by Zoom's ties to China.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020211123ehbn0004p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
